  "id": "q-methodology",
  "term": "Q methodology",
  "definition": "Q methodology is a research approach used to study people’s preferences by examining how they judge or sort stimuli that vary across multiple characteristics. In this application, it can be used to estimate which stimuli are preferred, which features matter most, and how these patterns differ between individuals.",
